## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop**: `newGame()` builds one state object; `rnd(S)` mulberry32 used for all randomness (terrain, colonists, events); `endTurn()` resolves 9 fixed steps in order. Score 2.

**F2 — Map**: 8x8 loop (`for y<8,x<8`) generates terrain from `rnd(S)`; `canBuild()` checks `b.terr.includes(tile.terr)`; `adj()` changes condenser water and forge/generator power output. Score 2.

**F3 — Economy**: chains water→soil→food (greenhouse case) and ore+power→metal (forge case); `cap()` caps enforced and overflow logged/clamped in step 8. Score 2.

**F4 — Population**: colonist objects `{skill,fatigue,morale,job,at}`; `workerMult()` reads `c.skill`, `c.fatigue`, `c.morale` for production. Score 2.

**F5 — Needs**: `fNeed`/`wNeed` consumed per turn; shortage sets `-12 morale`; `workerMult()` reads morale to cut output; morale recovers `+4` when needs met. Score 2.

**F6 — Research**: 10 `RES_NODES`; `buyResearch()` checks `n.pre`, deducts cost; each flag (`drills`,`hydro`,`turbines`,`smelt`,`fab`,`forecast`,`logistics`,`barter`,`medicine`,`scrub`) read in production/build/price code. Score 2.

**F7 — Events**: 12 `EVENTS`; weighted roll via `tot`/`roll` loop; 4 events (`refugees`,`sickness`,`mutiny`,`merchant`) have 2-3 choices with distinct state writes; `S.evcd[id]` cooldown filters eligible events. Score 2.

**F8 — Trade**: `price()` reads `S.r[g]/cap` and `S.market.drift[g]` (random-walked each turn); `market.stock/demand` limited; buy/sell both wired in `renderTrade` and `policy()`. Score 2.

**F9 — Hazard**: storm every 7th turn, `sev` scales with `S.turn`; damaged tiles excluded from production loop (`!t.dmg`); `walls`/`research.forecast` reduce `mit`; repair costs 2 parts and clears `dmg`. Score 2.

**F10 — Save/load**: `saveStr()`→textarea; `loadStr()` parses JSON, validates required fields/map length, returns `{err}` shown in UI. Score 2.

**F11 — End conditions**: `checkEnd()` sets `over='lose'` (pop 0) or `'win'` (turn>60,pop≥12,no shortage), both reachable; `score()` combines pop/research/stock/turns; summary table rendered when `G.over`. Score 2.

**F12 — UI**: `TABS` array with click handlers switch `tab`; `logi()` stores `t:S.turn` shown as `T#`; extensive `title=` tooltips; keydown handler for Space and 1-6; flex-wrap/minmax grid gives some narrow-screen adaptation. Score 2.

**F13 — Dev panel**: `runTests()` 18 real-invariant assertions (caps, prereqs, determinism, save/load, cooldowns, win/lose); `runHeadless()`+`policy()` run 200-turn headless sim printing `stateHash()`. Score 2.

**G1**: `S.research.drills` read in mine production, `S.research.hydro` in greenhouse, etc. — unlock directly changes yield formula each turn. Score 4.

**G2**: `S.shortF/S.shortW` set from consumption, applies `-12 morale`, then `workerMult()` zeroes/reduces output by `c.morale`. Score 4.

**G3**: storm sets `t.dmg=true`; production filters `!t.dmg` (zero output); repair button spends 2 parts, clears `dmg`, restoring output next turn. Score 4.

**G4**: `price()` formula reads `S.r[g]/cap(S,g)` (stockpile) and `S.market.drift[g]` (per-turn random walk in `endTurn` step 1). Score 4.

**G5**: `refugees` choice calls `addColonist`/mutates `S.col` morale/`S.r.food`; `sickness` choice mutates `S.r.parts` or colonist fatigue/morale — real state writes, not log-only. Score 4.

